// Distributed schedule for example 26-bin-min (TASK-0343.01.02).
//
// The MIN-combine (non-zero-identity) sibling of 08-histogram/
// distributed and 25-bin-parity/distributed. Mirrors them EXACTLY
// (i-band partition, whole-array replicate, host element-wise combine)
// — the load-bearing difference is the combine op AND its NON-ZERO
// identity: `bin_min` declares `combine=min`, whose identity is
// `i32::MAX`. Every per-worker partial AND the host `result` MUST
// pre-init to `i32::MAX` (not 0), and the host emits
// `result[_k] = result[_k].min(_tmp[_k])` (method form).
//
// Shape:
//   host    — owns I/O (load_key / load_val / save_output).
//   w0..w3  — each compute worker owns one i-band of the inputs and
//             min-folds it into a private FULL-width `result` (whole-
//             array replicate, pre-init i32::MAX). The compiler
//             partitions the outer `i` loop across the four workers via
//             partition=workers.
//
// Cross-worker edges:
//   key     host -> { w0..w3 }   (host loads, workers consume)
//   val     host -> { w0..w3 }   (host loads, workers consume)
//   result  { w0..w3 } -> host   (workers produce, host MIN-combines)
//
// Why the combine is sound: `min` is associative + commutative, and the
// i-band partition is a DISJOINT cover of the inputs — each input is
// min-folded into its bin exactly once, in exactly one worker's partial.
// A worker whose band contains no `key==b` keeps `result[b] == i32::MAX`
// (the identity), so the host `min(i32::MAX, ...)` correctly ignores it.
// The element-wise min of the 4 full partials equals the global per-bin
// minimum, independent of worker arrival order => bit-identical across
// all 7 tier-1 backends (PRD §10.1).
//
// All `sync` (the default transfer mode). `partition=workers` is the
// partition policy for the outer `i` loop — the same shape examples
// 03-reduction / 08-histogram / 25-bin-parity use.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // I/O on host.
    place load_key    on host;
    place load_val    on host;
    place save_output on host;

    // The pure step kernel distributed across compute workers.
    place bin_min on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Outer loop is the partition axis; one slice per compute worker.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // Cross-worker data — one transfer per data symbol that crosses.
    transfer key    : sync;
    transfer val    : sync;
    transfer result : sync;
}
